{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-matthew-025",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 25,
  "title": "Matthew 25",
  "display_title": "Matthew 25",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "matthew",
  "book": "Matthew",
  "bookName": "Matthew",
  "bookOrder": 40,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 25,
  "sortOrder": 40025,
  "verseCount": 46,
  "aliases": [
    "Matt",
    "Mt"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Then shall the kingdom of heaven be likened unto ten virgins, which took their lamps, and went forth to meet the bridegroom.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "And five of them were wise, and five were foolish.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "They that were foolish took their lamps, and took no oil with them:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "But the wise took oil in their vessels with their lamps.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "While the bridegroom tarried, they all slumbered and slept.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "And at midnight there was a cry made, Behold, the bridegroom cometh; go ye out to meet him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Then all those virgins arose, and trimmed their lamps.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "And the foolish said unto the wise, Give us of your oil; for our lamps are gone out.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "But the wise answered, saying, Not so; lest there be not enough for us and you: but go ye rather to them that sell, and buy for yourselves.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "And while they went to buy, the bridegroom came; and they that were ready went in with him to the marriage: and the door was shut.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Afterward came also the other virgins, saying, Lord, Lord, open to us.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "But he answered and said, Verily I say unto you, I know you not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Watch therefore, for ye know neither the day nor the hour wherein the Son of man cometh.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "For the kingdom of heaven is as a man travelling into a far country, who called his own servants, and delivered unto them his goods.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "And unto one he gave five talents, to another two, and to another one; to every man according to his several ability; and straightway took his journey.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Then he that had received the five talents went and traded with the same, and made them other five talents.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "And likewise he that had received two, he also gained other two.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "But he that had received one went and digged in the earth, and hid his lord’s money.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "After a long time the lord of those servants cometh, and reckoneth with them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "And so he that had received five talents came and brought other five talents, saying, Lord, thou deliveredst unto me five talents: behold, I have gained beside them five talents more.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "His lord said unto him, Well done, thou good and faithful servant: thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "He also that had received two talents came and said, Lord, thou deliveredst unto me two talents: behold, I have gained two other talents beside them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "His lord said unto him, Well done, good and faithful servant; thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Then he which had received the one talent came and said, Lord, I knew thee that thou art an hard man, reaping where thou hast not sown, and gathering where thou hast not strawed:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "And I was afraid, and went and hid thy talent in the earth: lo, there thou hast that is thine.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "His lord answered and said unto him, Thou wicked and slothful servant, thou knewest that I reap where I sowed not, and gather where I have not strawed:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Thou oughtest therefore to have put my money to the exchangers, and then at my coming I should have received mine own with usury.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Take therefore the talent from him, and give it unto him which hath ten talents.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "For unto every one that hath shall be given, and he shall have abundance: but from him that hath not shall be taken away even that which he hath.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "And cast ye the unprofitable servant into outer darkness: there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "When the Son of man shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "And before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another, as a shepherd divideth his sheep from the goats:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "And he shall set the sheep on his right hand, but the goats on the left.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "Then shall the King say unto them on his right hand, Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "For I was an hungred, and ye gave me meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me drink: I was a stranger, and ye took me in:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-036",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 36,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:36",
      "numberLabel": "36",
      "text": "Naked, and ye clothed me: I was sick, and ye visited me: I was in prison, and ye came unto me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:36",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:36"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-037",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 37,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:37",
      "numberLabel": "37",
      "text": "Then shall the righteous answer him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee an hungred, and fed thee? or thirsty, and gave thee drink?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:37",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:37"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-038",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 38,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:38",
      "numberLabel": "38",
      "text": "When saw we thee a stranger, and took thee in? or naked, and clothed thee?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:38",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:38"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-039",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 39,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:39",
      "numberLabel": "39",
      "text": "Or when saw we thee sick, or in prison, and came unto thee?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:39",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:39"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-040",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 40,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:40",
      "numberLabel": "40",
      "text": "And the King shall answer and say unto them, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it unto me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:40",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:40"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-041",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 41,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:41",
      "numberLabel": "41",
      "text": "Then shall he say also unto them on the left hand, Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:41",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-042",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 42,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:42",
      "numberLabel": "42",
      "text": "For I was an hungred, and ye gave me no meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me no drink:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:42",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:42"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-043",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 43,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:43",
      "numberLabel": "43",
      "text": "I was a stranger, and ye took me not in: naked, and ye clothed me not: sick, and in prison, and ye visited me not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:43",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:43"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-044",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 44,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:44",
      "numberLabel": "44",
      "text": "Then shall they also answer him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee an hungred, or athirst, or a stranger, or naked, or sick, or in prison, and did not minister unto thee?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:44",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:44"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-045",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 45,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:45",
      "numberLabel": "45",
      "text": "Then shall he answer them, saying, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye did it not to one of the least of these, ye did it not to me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:45",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:45"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-046",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 46,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:25:46",
      "numberLabel": "46",
      "text": "And these shall go away into everlasting punishment: but the righteous into life eternal.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 25:46",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:25:46"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
    "repository": "aruljohn/Bible-kjv",
